  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "isobus: Use a wmem_strbuf_t instead of snprintf",
  "description": "The second parameter is snprintf is the size of the buffer including\nthe terminating null; it writes up to bufsz - 1 characters (not\nincluding the terminating zero), unless bufsz is 0. Even though\nthe minute offset is supposed to be in the range -59 to 59, by the\ncalculation given it could be -100 or less, thus needing another\ncharacter. (In those cases it would be truncated to \"-100 mi\".)\n\nIt would be safe here to use 9 for the second parameter of snprintf,\nas the buffer does have size 9, but just use a wmem_strbuf_t instead.\n\nPrevents a format-truncation warning.\nPing #20175",
  "state": "merged",
